.TH SORTMEDIA 1 "August 2026" "sortmedia 0.2.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sortmedia \- sort photos and videos by recording date
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sortmedia
.PP
.B sortmedia
.B \-r
.PP
.B sortmedia
.BR \-c " " FILE
.RB [ \-c " " FILE ]...
.PP
.B sortmedia
.BR \-h | \-\-help | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sortmedia
reads recording dates from EXIF and video metadata and organizes media files
in configurable directory structures. ExifTool is used for metadata. If no
recording date exists, the filesystem creation time and then modification time
are used.
.PP
Sortmedia uses directory-local hidden TOML configuration, preserves embedded
metadata without re-encoding files, records completed operations for
hash-verified undo, and supports scripts through quiet and JSON output modes.
All analysis and file operations remain local to the machine.
.PP
Files sharing a base name are handled as a companion group. RAW+JPEG pairs,
Live Photo image+video pairs, and XMP, AAE, or THM sidecars are copied or moved
together without rewriting their contents or embedded metadata.
.PP
Each config file defines one independent job. Relative paths are resolved from
the config file's directory. Multiple config files run in command-line order.
.PP
When started without arguments in an interactive terminal, sortmedia opens a
menu for the current working directory. The menu can create a local
.I .sortmedia.toml
or run an existing one. It can also update the operation and directory layout
in the same config file while preserving all other settings and comments.
Non-interactive use requires
.BR \-\-config .
.PP
The main menu also contains an independent Live Photo cleanup tool. It lists
only image/video pairs with matching Apple ContentIdentifier or MediaGroupUUID metadata, shows
the paired image, video size, duration, and identifier, and excludes matches
based only on filenames. Typing MOVE sends the confirmed video companions to
recoverable .sortmedia/trash without sorting any files.
No config is required. The menu asks whether to include subdirectories and
defaults to yes.
.PP
Main-menu option 6 normalizes filenames in an existing library without a config
file or moving files between directories. It asks whether to include
subdirectories and defaults to yes. The built-in filename format is
date_time_original. Recognized date and time prefixes are removed before the
original-name field is rendered, preventing names from growing on repeated
runs. The complete rename plan is shown first, collisions abort the entire
plan, and typing RENAME is required. Completed renames are recorded in the
internal .sortmedia history for undo; no .sortmedia.toml is created.
.PP
Exact duplicate detection uses SHA-256 across filenames. Optional perceptual
matching combines structural, luminance, and color fingerprints. Dangerous
absolute or parent-traversing output templates are rejected, and existing
files are never overwritten.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r , " " \-\-run-local
Run
.I .sortmedia.toml
from the current working directory without opening the interactive menu.
.TP
.BR \-c " " FILE , " " \-\-config " " FILE
Read a job from FILE. FILE must be a hidden TOML file such as
.IR .sortmedia.toml .
This option may be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-f " " DIRECTORY , " " \-\-folder " " DIRECTORY
Override the source directory, or run without a config file using command-line
defaults.
.TP
.BR \-d " " DIRECTORY , " " \-\-destination " " DIRECTORY
Override the destination directory.
.TP
.BR \-R , " " \-\-recursive
Scan source subdirectories.
.TP
.B \-\-no-recursive
Do not scan source subdirectories.
.TP
.BR \-\-preview , " " \-\-copy , " " \-\-move
Override the operation for the current run.
.TP
.BR \-\-layout " " TEMPLATE
Override the directory layout.
.TP
.BR \-\-filename " " TEMPLATE
Override the filename template.
.TP
.BR \-\-duplicates " " hash|rename|skip
Override duplicate handling.
.TP
.B \-\-perceptual
Detect visually similar images using a difference hash in addition to exact
SHA-256 duplicate detection.
.TP
.BR \-q , " " \-\-quiet
Suppress normal output.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit newline-delimited JSON events for automation.
.TP
.BR \-\-max-depth " " N
Limit recursive scanning to N directory levels. Zero scans only the source.
.TP
.B \-\-history
List structured run journals stored under .sortmedia/history.
.TP
.BR \-\-undo " " [RUN_ID]
Undo the latest completed run, or the selected run. Destination content is
verified with SHA-256 before it is removed or moved back.
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-\-help
Show built-in help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the program version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.nf
folder = "incoming"
destination = "."
recursive = false
operation = "preview"
layout = "{year}/{month}/{day}"
filename = "{date}_{time}_{original}"
duplicates = "hash"
timezone = "local"
.fi
.TP
.B folder
Source directory. The config directory is used when omitted.
.TP
.B destination
Destination directory for the sorted structure.
.TP
.B recursive
Whether to scan source subdirectories.
.TP
.B operation
.BR preview , " " copy , " or " move .
The default is
.BR preview .
.TP
.B layout
Directory template. Available fields include year, month, day, date, time,
original, and extension.
.PP
The interactive create and update menus describe common choices as
.BR {year} ,
.BR {year}/{month} ,
and
.BR {year}/{month}/{day} ,
with example output for each choice.
.TP
.B filename
Filename template. The original extension is preserved.
.TP
.B timezone
Output timezone: local, UTC, or an IANA name such as Europe/Oslo.
.TP
.B live_photo_videos
Controls metadata-confirmed Live Photo video companions: include sorts the
video with the image, leave keeps it in the source, and trash moves it to
recoverable
.IR .sortmedia/trash .
Leave and trash require an identical Apple ContentIdentifier in the image and
video; matching filenames alone are insufficient.
.TP
.B duplicates
.B hash
compares SHA-256 content, skips identical files even when names differ, and
renames filename collisions whose content differs;
.B rename
adds a numeric suffix on collision;
.B skip
skips the file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cd /media/import && sortmedia -r
sortmedia -r --move --recursive
sortmedia -f /media/camera -d /photos --copy
sortmedia -c /media/import/.sortmedia.toml
sortmedia -c ~/photos/.sortmedia.toml -c /media/camera/.import.toml
.fi
.SH SAFETY
Use
.B operation = "preview"
before copy or move. Existing files are never overwritten. System-wide
installation does not bypass Linux permissions on source or destination files.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
indicates success.
.B 1
indicates a configuration, filesystem, or program error.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Python 3.10 or newer, a TOML parser, and ExifTool.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/bin/sortmedia
.br
.I /usr/lib/sortmedia
.br
.I /usr/share/man/man1/sortmedia.1.gz
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR exiftool (1),
.BR crontab (5)
